  "findings": [
    "&#1114111; is a valid Java class label (exit 0, empty stderr, real CLASS diagram). The tip CLI exits 1: 'An invalid XML character (Unicode: 0xdfff)'. apply_amp_diese pushes char::from_u32(1114111), which is U+10FFFF. java_utf16 reserves U+10F800..=U+10FFFF as carriers for unpaired surrogates, and carried_unit(U+10FFFF) is 0xDFFF, so svg_export rejects the label. The registered probe tim-builtin-value-boundaries/checker-claude-round5/cr_ent_dec_10fffd.puml is the same hole one scalar down: class \"Vault &#1114109; end\" (U+10FFFD). Base CLI exits 0. Tip CLI exits 1 reporting 0xdffd. Strict compare of the tip stdout fails to parse. Base already missed that golden (6 diffs) and still produced a diagram.",
    "U+00C6 is the right character and the wrong advance. Activity size 12, 'Step Sable \u00c6': Java textLength 74.4609, tip 71.8594. Title size 14, 'Title Thor \u00c6': Java 89.4346, tip 86.3379. Component size 14, 'Face \u00c6': Java 47.332, tip 44.2969. The ASCII label 'Comp Core' in that component diagram matches at 76.4121. Whole-output strict compare still fails (activity 10 diffs, chrome 3, component 1). The maker declared this residue for U+2028 and U+2029. \u00c6 is the same class on a held-out letter. U+1F389 in ckg6_five_decimal_emoji does match, so the hole is not every supplementary scalar.",
    "&#128; on the class name Zed&#128;ora decodes to U+0080 in both the Java SVG and the tip SVG. The fill set is {#F1F1F1, #ADD1B2, #000000} on Java, base, and tip. textLength is 54.9199 versus 54.8652 (delta 0.0547, outside GEOM_EPS 0.02). This probe does not reproduce parse_entity_colors reading #233 out of &#233;. That residue remains the maker's ref_class_eacute_amp, one fill diff, reconfirmed on the CH re-score.",
    "Ten held-out probes strict-match at the tip and failed at the base: leading zeros, adjacent references, five-digit emoji, a color argument, !define plus a TIM assignment, <U+0024> and <U+005C>, tilde forms, a link tooltip, a class stereotype with a mono member, and a WBS node. Lost strict matches on the 48-probe batch: 0. Forms Java does not convert match at both trees: &#x41;, bare &#;, <u+0044> and <U+010041>, and a reference split by Creole. CH re-score with these binaries against the maker's immutable Java results: 13/20 tip matches (the maker's match list) and 1/20 at the base. Separator probes and ref_class_eacute_amp stay misses. ref_invalid_uplus_nul is an INVALID crash page; the tip stdout contains a NUL.",
    "&#36;, &#92;, &#55296;, and &#1114112; are exit-0 Java crash pages (Illegal group reference, character to be escaped is missing, invalid surrogate d800, not a valid code point 0x110000). They are INVALID. Base and tip stdout are byte-identical. &#0; is an exit-0 crash page for XML 0x0. The tip emits a raw NUL, so the comparator cannot parse the stdout. That change is on invalid input.",
    "Timing, gantt, salt, JSON, YAML, and nwdiag probes are byte-identical base versus tip and still fail strict compare. Those emitters do not call push_literal, so the conversion never runs. Missing-emoji <:ckg6_nope:> stays literal beside a converted &#80;; Java splits the emoji fallback. That gap is pre-existing and the nearby reference did convert."
  ],
